# Docs and Release Rules

- Keep public docs user-focused and contributor docs contract-focused.
- `CHANGELOG.md` must avoid code jargon, filenames, and internal architecture details.
- Review `docs/CI_AND_RELEASE.md` before changing workflows, packaging, version bumps, or release process.
- For GitHub CLI bodies longer than one sentence, write an ignored markdown body file and use `--body-file`.
- Never merge PRs or create release tags unless the user explicitly directs that exact action.
